From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: departed nodes age out of the database like departed clients

agent rows were written and refreshed but never deleted (the schema
comment on last_seen said so verbatim), so a decommissioned node lived
in the database forever and db_restore() revived it as a ghost on every
boot, where the live model then spent 65 s aging it out again. The
2026-08-04 review flagged this as finding 1.13; the reliability plan
carries it as item 1.5 ("the departed list grows forever, a retired
node comes back to life on every boot").

Reuse the client policy wholesale: the hourly janitor deletes agents
whose last_seen is older than MAPC_DB_HISTORY_DAYS (20 days). A node
that is merely power-cycled or offline for days is untouched - reviving
such a node is the recovery guarantee this database exists for. Only a
node gone for weeks is treated as decommissioned.

The schema has no ON DELETE CASCADE, so the janitor deletes children
first, all keyed off one doomed-agents set: the MLD subgraph (apmld,
affiliated_ap, ttlm, bstamld, affiliated_bsta), clients whose last
owner was the doomed node (sta, and sta_mld/affiliated_sta via the
doomed node\x27s AP-MLDs), the radio subtree (radio_caps,
operating_class, scan_result, bss, radio), both directions of
topology_link, neighbor entries, and the 1905 security row. The
controller\x27s own agent row is excluded by construction.

The client-MLD family also gains the retention it was missing: sta_mld
has its own last_seen but no janitor rule; it now follows the same
20-day cutoff (affiliated_sta rows go with their sta_mld).

Verify on hardware: insert a fake agent row with last_seen 21 days old
plus a radio/bss child, run one janitor cycle (or wait for the hourly
tick), confirm the whole subtree is gone while all live nodes and the
controller row survive; then reboot and confirm db_restore no longer
logs the ghost.
--- a/src/db/mapc_sync.c
+++ b/src/db/mapc_sync.c
@@ -1818,6 +1818,63 @@
 		stmt_finish(c->db, st);
 	}
 
+	/* Departed NODES age out the same way departed clients do. agent rows
+	 * were written and refreshed but never deleted, so a decommissioned
+	 * node lived in the database forever and db_restore() revived it as a
+	 * ghost on every boot. A node unseen for MAPC_DB_HISTORY_DAYS is
+	 * gone for good; a power-cycled or briefly-offline node is untouched,
+	 * which is the recovery guarantee this database exists for.
+	 *
+	 * No ON DELETE CASCADE in the schema, so children go first, keyed off
+	 * the same doomed set. The controller's own row is never doomed. */
+#define DOOMED_AGENTS \
+	"(SELECT almac FROM agent WHERE COALESCE(last_seen,0) < ?1 " \
+	"AND almac <> COALESCE((SELECT controller_almac FROM network LIMIT 1),''))"
+#define DOOMED_RADIOS "(SELECT ruid FROM radio WHERE agent_almac IN " DOOMED_AGENTS ")"
+#define DOOMED_APMLDS "(SELECT mld_macaddr FROM apmld WHERE agent_almac IN " DOOMED_AGENTS ")"
+	{
+		static const char * const doom_sql[] = {
+			"DELETE FROM affiliated_sta WHERE mld_macaddr IN "
+			"(SELECT mld_macaddr FROM sta_mld WHERE ap_mld_macaddr IN " DOOMED_APMLDS ")",
+			"DELETE FROM sta_mld WHERE ap_mld_macaddr IN " DOOMED_APMLDS,
+			"DELETE FROM ttlm WHERE mld_macaddr IN " DOOMED_APMLDS,
+			"DELETE FROM affiliated_ap WHERE mld_macaddr IN " DOOMED_APMLDS,
+			"DELETE FROM apmld WHERE agent_almac IN " DOOMED_AGENTS,
+			"DELETE FROM affiliated_bsta WHERE mld_macaddr IN "
+			"(SELECT mld_macaddr FROM bstamld WHERE agent_almac IN " DOOMED_AGENTS ")",
+			"DELETE FROM bstamld WHERE agent_almac IN " DOOMED_AGENTS,
+			"DELETE FROM sta WHERE agent_almac IN " DOOMED_AGENTS,
+			"DELETE FROM radio_caps WHERE ruid IN " DOOMED_RADIOS,
+			"DELETE FROM operating_class WHERE ruid IN " DOOMED_RADIOS,
+			"DELETE FROM scan_result WHERE ruid IN " DOOMED_RADIOS,
+			"DELETE FROM bss WHERE ruid IN " DOOMED_RADIOS,
+			"DELETE FROM radio WHERE agent_almac IN " DOOMED_AGENTS,
+			"DELETE FROM topology_link WHERE child_almac IN " DOOMED_AGENTS
+			" OR parent_almac IN " DOOMED_AGENTS,
+			"DELETE FROM neighbor WHERE neighbor IN " DOOMED_AGENTS
+			" OR next_hop IN " DOOMED_AGENTS,
+			"DELETE FROM ieee1905_security WHERE id IN " DOOMED_AGENTS,
+			"DELETE FROM agent WHERE COALESCE(last_seen,0) < ?1 "
+			"AND almac <> COALESCE((SELECT controller_almac FROM network LIMIT 1),'')",
+			/* client-MLD family has its own last_seen: same retention */
+			"DELETE FROM affiliated_sta WHERE mld_macaddr IN "
+			"(SELECT mld_macaddr FROM sta_mld WHERE COALESCE(last_seen,0) < ?1)",
+			"DELETE FROM sta_mld WHERE COALESCE(last_seen,0) < ?1",
+		};
+		size_t i;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < sizeof(doom_sql)/sizeof(doom_sql[0]); i++) {
+			st = NULL;
+			if (mapdb_prepare(c->db, doom_sql[i], &st) == MAPDB_OK) {
+				mapdb_bind_int(st, 1, cutoff);
+				stmt_finish(c->db, st);
+			}
+		}
+	}
+#undef DOOMED_APMLDS
+#undef DOOMED_RADIOS
+#undef DOOMED_AGENTS
+
 	st = NULL;
 	if (mapdb_prepare(c->db,
 			  "DELETE FROM sta_metrics_hist WHERE rowid NOT IN "
--- a/src/db/mapdb_schema.h
+++ b/src/db/mapdb_schema.h
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@
 	"    max_aplink_num       INTEGER,\n"
 	"    max_bstalink_num     INTEGER,\n"
 	"    tid_link_caps        INTEGER,\n"
-	"    last_seen            INTEGER             -- last_tsp_seen epoch [cntlr.h:188]; updated, never used to DELETE\n"
+	"    last_seen            INTEGER             -- last_tsp_seen epoch [cntlr.h:188]; drives departed-node ageout\n"
 	");\n"
 	"\n"
 	"-- 4. radios (iopsys wifi_radio_element)\n"
